WEBVTT

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:04.500
Architecture models organize ICS functions so teams can discuss dependencies,

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:06.560
trust boundaries, and required communication.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.400
At the field level, sensors and actuators interact with the physical process.

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:13.950
The control level contains PLCs, RTUs, and other controllers.

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:17.500
Supervisory systems provide operator views and higher-level coordination.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:22.435
Above direct supervision, operations systems may include historians, application servers,

00:00:22.435 --> 00:00:25.955
engineering services, production management, and site administration.

00:00:25.955 --> 00:00:29.800
Enterprise systems consume selected information and provide services such as identity,

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:31.500
business planning, or support.

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:34.565
These connections are useful, but they must be explicit and controlled.

00:00:34.565 --> 00:00:38.100
The Purdue model is a common reference for describing these functional layers.

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:41.980
It can help identify how a connection crosses from enterprise activity toward site

00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:43.300
operations and control.

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:45.800
It is not a perfect map of every modern environment,

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:49.565
and it should not replace a site-specific architecture or data-flow analysis.

00:00:49.565 --> 00:00:53.800
An industrial DMZ is commonly placed between enterprise and industrial operations.

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:57.900
It can host intermediary services such as jump systems, remote-access brokers,

00:00:57.900 --> 00:01:00.900
update staging, file transfer, or historian replication.

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:02.380
The objective is to avoid broad,

00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:06.100
direct connections while creating monitored points for necessary exchange.

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:09.450
Segmentation groups assets by function, criticality, and trust.

00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:12.970
Controlled conduits permit only required communication between zones.

00:01:12.970 --> 00:01:17.400
Good design also accounts for redundancy, failover, management access, vendor support,

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:21.040
safety systems, and what happens when a boundary device is unavailable.

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:22.800
Architecture is a living operational record.

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:26.300
Validate diagrams against observed traffic and engineering knowledge,

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:30.060
document serial and wireless paths, assign owners, and update changes.

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:34.440
A useful model helps teams predict consequence, place controls, investigate movement,

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:38.100
and coordinate recovery without assuming that every site follows the same layered pattern.
